/* 2026-07-07 user-confirmed: .mc-cart-float__icon is the duplicate/oversized
   SVG documented at "CART GLYPH ALIGNMENT" further down this file —
   template.min.js's [class*=mc-cart-float] selector also matches this inner
   svg and force-sizes it to 52px via inline !important every ~100ms,
   independent of the anchor. This CSS rule alone can't hold against that
   interval (confirmed live: reverts within ~100ms) — the real fix is a
   MutationObserver in mc-plp-enforcer.js that re-applies display:none
   instantly and ALSO paints the cart glyph as an inline background-image on
   the anchor (the background-image rule further down THIS file turned out
   to be losing a cascade fight against other unrelated rules setting
   background-image:initial on the same anchor — confirmed live the icon
   went completely blank without the JS-driven inline background-image).
   This rule stays only as a first-paint assist before the JS runs. */
.mc-cart-float__icon,
.mc-cart-float__icon path {
  display: none !important;
}

