   Root cause of the "giant chevron" bug reported on every mobile PDP:
   a full audit found 33 separate rules throughout this file that target
   #display_menu_1 / .mc-header-desktop-bar with NO @media guard — many
   labeled "(DESKTOP/TABLET)" in their own comments but never actually
   scoped. The highest-specificity offender uses a doubled ID
   (#display_menu_1#display_menu_1, specificity 2 IDs) to deliberately
   "outrank the site's own single-ID rules" — including the mobile
   display:none rule that's supposed to hide this nav on phones. Net
   effect: the full desktop nav (absolutely positioned, with hover-only
   dropdown submenu carets meant for mouse users) rendered on every
   mobile viewport, overlapping page content with oversized icons.
   Two of the worst offenders were scoped to desktop-only directly
   (~line 963 PDP block, ~line 20002 RH-STYLE HEADER NAV block), but
   given 33 total instances scattered across ~21,000 lines, hunting
   down every one individually risks missing some and breaking desktop
   nav styling in the process. Instead: this block sits at the very end
   of the file (wins any specificity tie via source order) and matches
   the doubled-ID specificity exactly (plus a doubled class for the
   desktop bar), guaranteeing the mobile hide always wins regardless of
   how many older unscoped rules still exist upstream. */
