/* 2026-07-07 shopping cart page (shoppingcart.asp) mobile fix — CONSOLIDATED
   final version. Superseded five iterative attempts (table-squeeze,
   flex-column stack, ::before labels, text-align overrides) that are no
   longer in the file; each is summarized here only where it explains a
   non-obvious choice below.

   Root problem: legacy Volusion cart row markup is a single <tr> with 12
   <td> cells — image, description, "each" price, qty input, "total"
   price, and a remove button, interleaved with empty divider/spacer cells
   (most of the 12) — all originally laid out via table-layout:auto, which
   starved the description column to 74px while an unused spacer/total
   column hogged width, and caused mid-word text wrapping and horizontal
   overflow past the viewport on every mobile width tested (confirmed
   live: 74px description column, 172px oversized total column, RECALCULATE
   and shipping fields cut off past the right edge).

   User explicitly wants: product name + each price + qty on ONE line,
   total on the line beneath. Reaching that requires CSS Grid (not flexbox
   — flex-wrap's automatic line-breaking based on available space produced
   unpredictable wrapping when tested live) with named grid-areas, which
   let the 12 DOM-order cells be placed into an arbitrary 2D layout
   regardless of source order:
     row 1: image (centered, spans full width)
     row 2: description | each price | qty        <- same line, as requested
     row 3: total                                  <- beneath, as requested
     row 4: remove button
   All the empty spacer/divider cells are hidden outright (nth-child
   1,2,5,7,9,12 — verified live via full cell dump, they carry no content).

   Two structural blockers found and fixed along the way:
   1) Percentage widths don't resolve reliably for a flex/grid/block
      element whose containing block is still a table context — the
      enclosing <table> and <tbody> must ALSO be forced to display:block
      (confirmed live: without this, width:100% on the row computed to
      93px instead of ~550px). Same fix pattern as the Saranoni PDP layout
      earlier in this file.
   2) Each/total values and the qty input are wrapped several layers deep
      in legacy markup (<table width="75"><tr><td><div align="right">...,
      qty in <table><tr><td><center><input>). Overriding one layer at a
      time (inline-table, text-align:left) kept losing to whatever the
      next wrapper down did. display:contents on every descendant of
      those three cells removes ALL the wrapper elements from the layout
      tree at once (their children render as if directly inside the
      cell), leaving only the actual text nodes and the qty <input> as
      real boxes — which is what finally let "Each: $799" etc. render as
      single, cleanly-aligned lines instead of stacked or disconnected
      fragments. Confirmed live at 666px: product name/each/qty share one
      row, total sits on its own row beneath, no overflow
      (scrollWidth 646 < innerWidth 666), no mid-word wrapping. */
@media (max-width: 991px) {
  html.shoppingcart table:has(tr.v65-cart-details-row),
  html.shoppingcart table:has(tr.v65-cart-details-row) tbody {
    display: block !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    table-layout: auto !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart select {
    max-width: 100% !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    font-size: 13px !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart input[type="text"] {
    max-width: 100% !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart td.v65-cart-header-text,
  html.shoppingcart td.v65-cart-header-blank {
    display: none !important;
  }
  /* 2026-07-07 follow-up 6: user reported white gaps between the grey
     card sections and asked for Total right-aligned. The gaps came from
     CSS Grid's row-gap/column-gap rendering as literal empty space that
     shows the grid CONTAINER's background, not each item's — the row
     (tr) was transparent while every cell had its own rgb(238,238,238)
     grey, so the 4-8px gaps between grid areas showed white page
     background through. Confirmed live via computed background-color:
     row was rgba(0,0,0,0), cells were rgb(238,238,238). Giving the row
     itself the same grey makes the whole card read as one seamless
     block regardless of gap size.

     2026-07-07 follow-up 7: user sent an actual phone screenshot (not
     achievable through this session's testing — resize_window has been
     stuck reporting 666px innerWidth all session regardless of requested
     width, a tooling limitation, so every prior "verified live" check in
     this file was only ever tested at 666px) showing genuine overflow:
     Total, Qty, RECALCULATE, and shipping fields all cut off on a real
     narrow phone. Root cause: grid-template-columns was "auto auto 1fr"
     for the desc/each/qty row — "auto" tracks size to their content's
     max-content width and do NOT shrink below it, so "Molly Olson
     5-Piece Dining Set" forced its column to its full unwrapped text
     width regardless of how little viewport space was actually
     available. Fine at 666px, genuinely overflows narrower. Fixed by
     making the DESCRIPTION column the shrinkable one
     (minmax(0, 1fr) instead of auto) so it wraps/shrinks to whatever
     space is left after each/qty (short, naturally-fixed-width content)
     take theirs, instead of forcing the row wider than the viewport. */
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row {
    display: grid !important;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(0, auto) minmax(0, auto) !important;
    grid-template-areas:
      "img img img"
      "desc each qty"
      "total total total"
      "remove remove remove" !important;
    column-gap: 8px !important;
    row-gap: 4px !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    max-width: 100% !important;
    background-color: rgb(238, 238, 238) !important;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd !important;
    padding: 12px 0 !important;
    align-items: center !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td {
    display: block !important;
    box-sizing: border-box !important;
    text-align: left !important;
    word-break: normal !important;
    overflow-wrap: normal !important;
  }
  /* Empty spacer/divider cells Volusion renders alongside each real
     column — verified live via full cell dump (12 total, only 6 carry
     content). */
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(1),
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(2),
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(5),
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(7),
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(9),
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(12) {
    display: none !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td.v65-cart-detail-productimage {
    grid-area: img !important;
    width: 100px !important;
    max-width: 100px !important;
    margin: 0 auto 4px !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart td.v65-cart-detail-productimage img {
    width: 100% !important;
    height: auto !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td.v65-cart-detail-productimage + td {
    grid-area: desc !important;
    font-size: 13px !important;
    font-weight: 600 !important;
    min-width: 0 !important;
    overflow-wrap: break-word !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(6) {
    grid-area: each !important;
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center !important;
    gap: 4px !important;
    white-space: nowrap !important;
    font-size: 13px !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(8) {
    grid-area: qty !important;
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center !important;
    gap: 4px !important;
    white-space: nowrap !important;
    font-size: 13px !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(10) {
    grid-area: total !important;
    display: flex !important;
    align-items: center !important;
    justify-content: flex-end !important;
    text-align: right !important;
    gap: 4px !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(11) {
    grid-area: remove !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(6)::before {
    content: "Each: ";
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #666;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(8)::before {
    content: "Qty: ";
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #666;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(10)::before {
    content: "Total: ";
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #666;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(6) *,
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(8) *,
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(10) * {
    display: contents !important;
  }
  html.shoppingcart tr.v65-cart-details-row > td:nth-child(8) input {
    display: inline-block !important;
    width: 32px !important;
  }
}
/* 2026-07-07 follow-up 7 continued: the CSS above (minmax grid columns,
