   (same-origin iframe at a real 390px viewport) found a second, deeper
   bug: this table's label column and value column split ~276px/~31px
   regardless of ANY width rule tried on the cells — not just CSS
   (stylesheet, `!important`), but even inline `style.setProperty(...,
   'important')` set directly via JS on the row's own cells made zero
   difference to the rendered box (confirmed via getBoundingClientRect
   before/after in the same synchronous call, so it wasn't a timing/cache
   issue). Even an explicit <colgroup><col width=45%><col width=55%>
   only partially worked (one column moved, the other didn't). This
   table's column-width resolution is resistant to essentially every
   normal CSS technique for controlling it — same family of issue as the
   nested-table width problem solved via JS pixel-width elsewhere in this
   file, just immune to that fix too since this isn't a container-width
   problem, it's a column-split problem.

