   all. Force the table/rows/cells to `display:block`, so each label and
   its field stack vertically (full width) instead of sitting side by
   side — sidesteps the column-width bug entirely instead of fighting it.
   This is the same approach the original 2026-07-07 comment above
   already flagged as "the real fix" for the truncated-select problem,
   just not applied until this table proved unfixable any other way.
   Verified live: Country/Zip fields render at 302px wide (full width, no
   more "United St..." truncation either), radios at a clean 16px, all
   content within x:377 of the 389px viewport, body.scrollWidth 374 (no
   horizontal overflow). */
