/* 2026-07-09 SARANONI PDP MOBILE — options-column nested-table overflow.
   User reported (mobile only, Saranoni products only — e.g. Bamboni
   Socks): color swatches rendering below the ADD TO CART button instead
   of above "Product Details", the ATC button not fully visible/not
   centered, and the brand logo not centered.

   Root cause, confirmed live (same-origin iframe, real 386-390px
   viewport): td.mc-pdp-options-td (already display:block via an earlier
   rule) sits inside a legacy Volusion <table><tbody><tr> chain where the
   immediate parent <tr> was still display:table-row — a display-mode
   mismatch between a block child and its table-row parent that produces
   nonsensical anonymous-box sizing (measured live: the child TD rendered
   WIDER than several of its own ancestors, e.g. a 340px child inside a
   48px-wide ancestor TBODY). Forcing every level in that chain to
   display:block, using :has() so the whole chain (however many levels
   deep) is caught in one rule, fixed it: logo/purchase-stack/ATC button
   all moved from overflowing the viewport by ~13px to fitting with
   margin to spare, AND — without any separate ordering/flex rule needed
   — the color-swatch-wrapper and #mc-pdp-accordion already came out in
   the correct visual order (swatch above accordion) once the broken
   anonymous-box rendering was removed. (A flex + explicit `order`
   approach was tried first to force the order directly, but it
   regressed the width fix in testing — this simpler :has() rule alone
   was sufficient and didn't have that side effect.) */
@media (max-width: 991px) {
  html body.mc-saranoni-pdp table:has(td.mc-pdp-options-td),
  html body.mc-saranoni-pdp tbody:has(td.mc-pdp-options-td),
  html body.mc-saranoni-pdp tr:has(td.mc-pdp-options-td) {
    display: block !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    max-width: 100% !important;
    table-layout: auto !important;
  }
}

